From 437c8bc2a4814e2ee5a7226cd93c7fba09a42cce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:14:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wallet(v2): map V2 wire outputs back to the wallet's own
 scripts

After a restart, a wallet that had mined 101 blocks and sent a few
transactions listed only the sends in listtransactions, while
getwalletinfo still counted every transaction. Its balance was zero,
gettransaction showed coinbases with no details, and rescanblockchain
found nothing.

The miner adapts its coinbase outputs to V2 form: the in-memory CTxOut
keeps the legacy scriptPubKey alongside a single branch,
BranchLeaf(script). The V2 wire serialization (v2/031) carries only the
branch, so every deserialized copy of such an output (the wallet
database on load, a block read from disk while the wallet catches up or
rescans, a block or transaction from a peer) has the synthetic 45-byte
wire script from CTxOut::FromV2Output (v2/045). The inherited wallet
only knows its legacy scripts, so IsMine failed for these outputs. Before
the restart the wallet still held the miner's in-memory transactions,
which is why the problem appeared only afterwards. Transactions the
wallet creates are unaffected: their outputs have no branches and are
serialized with their scripts.

Each ScriptPubKeyMan now answers GetScriptForV2Branch from an index of
the scripts it recognizes, rebuilt when they change. For the legacy
manager these are P2PK and P2PKH for every key and watched pubkey, P2SH
for every redeem script, and every watch-only script; for the
descriptor manager, its scriptPubKey map. CWallet::WithV2OutputScripts
restores the script of each plain single-branch output that the wallet
knows. This leaves the TxId, TxHash and wire bytes unchanged, which the
function checks. AddToWalletIfInvolvingMe applies it to every incoming
transaction, and LoadWallet applies it to every loaded transaction
once keys and scripts are loaded, since transaction records come
first in the database.

wallet_v2_output_scripts.py checks, across a restart with the same
datadir, that listtransactions is unchanged and agrees with txcount,
and that balances survive. It also checks that a restored coinbase can
be spent, that blocks mined while the wallet was unloaded are found on
load, and that a rescan from disk lists the same transactions. Without
this change the test fails at the first check (6 entries instead of
107).

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/031)
